Experiment                    : starts at 2026-10-22 10:00:17.685602 (67959.4856577)
Experiment                    : This experiment compares run time and resource consumption of TPC-DS queries in different DBMS.
TPC-DS (SF=1) data is loaded and benchmark is executed.
Query ordering is Q1 - Q99.
All instances use the same query parameters.
Timeout per query is 1200. A reset script (e.g. CHECKPOINT/VACUUM) runs before each benchmarking round.
Import sets indexes and constraints after loading and recomputes statistics.
Load durability is relaxed (-xld; restored after the load).
Experiment uses bexhoma version 0.11.7.
Experiment is limited to DBMS ['MariaDB'].
Import is handled by 8 processes (pods).
Loading is fixed to cl-worker38.
Benchmarking is fixed to cl-worker38.
SUT is fixed to cl-worker36.
Loading is tested with [8] threads, split into [8] pods.
Benchmarking is tested with [1] threads, split into [1] pods.
Benchmarking is run as [1, 2] times the number of benchmarking pods.
Experiment is run once.
Maximum DBMS across the whole cluster is 10.
Results are validated against basic correctness requirements.
SUT requests 4 CPU and 16Gi RAM.
